    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The po-boy is always 'dressed': shredded lettuce, sliced tomato, and sauce. The remoulade sauce is sharp and spicy, not the mild French version. It is made with mayonnaise, mustard, hot sauce, capers, and lemon juice. The prawns are coated in a seasoned cornmeal and flour mix and fried in hot oil: they need to be crispy, not soggy."
          }
        ]
      },
